# Ticket state contract

One file per tested ticket: `tickets/{ID}.md`. The YAML frontmatter is
machine-readable state; the body is evidence. An agent returning after a week
reads the frontmatter and knows exactly where to continue.

## Frontmatter (all keys required; `tools/tickets/validate.py` enforces it)

```yaml
---
id: PROJ-123
title: Short human title
scope: api            # api|ui-web|mobile|backend|multi-surface|tooling
status: analyzed      # see state machine
verdict: null         # null until done, then pass|partial|fail
build: null           # version/branch/commit tested, or null
environment: staging  # dev|staging|prod|null — prod is read-only for agents
tracker: https://tracker.example/browse/PROJ-123
design: null          # design link or null
source_refs: []       # files reviewed (path[:line]); pins the implementation
started: 2026-01-01
updated: 2026-01-01   # bump on EVERY write
next_action: "One concrete step a fresh agent can execute immediately"
blockers: []          # strings; [] when none
---
```

`next_action` and `blockers` are the resume payload. Specific, never vague:
"run the negative matrix on device once a non-DE account exists", not
"continue testing".

## State machine

```
analyzing → analyzed → planned → in_test → reporting → done
                 ↔ blocked (from any active state; reason in blockers)
```

- Create the file at the end of analysis (`analyzed`), not at the end of the run.
- Update `status`, `updated`, `next_action`, `blockers` at every phase boundary.
- Blocked: set `status: blocked`, record why, set `next_action` to the unblock step.
- `verdict: pass` requires execution evidence in the body. No green without a run.
- Never delete a ticket file. Supersede by updating it.

## Body sections, in order

Analysis (requirements, source review with `[SEVERITY]` risks, locator or
endpoint table) → Test plan (per scenario: automated | manual | blocked) →
Execution & results (real output, xfail/skip with reasons) → Handoff (mirrors
`next_action`) → Tracker comment (format from `tracker-reporting.mdc`) → Notes.
Start from `tickets/_TEMPLATE.md`.
